---
title: ChromaClack - The Good The Bad and The Ugly
publishedDate: 2026-09-24
excerpt: >-
  A retrospective on two weeks of failed effort in trying to implement a multi
  axis input element, that would allow a user to explore colour theory.
---
> "Never promise to do the possible. Anyone could do the possible. You should promise to do the impossible, because sometimes the impossible was possible, if you could find the right way, and at least you could often extend the limits of the possible. And if you failed, well, it had been impossible."  — Terry Pratchett, *Going Postal*

\**

After getting this blog site up and running, and my fancy pants Hello World project finished, I decided to pick something more difficult for my next project. I wanted to test the limits of what I could achieve when coding with AI, so I decided to pick a domain that I felt would be challenging and outside of the comfort zone. The idea I came up with was ChromaClack, a toy app that allows the user to explore colour theory through a single UI element. This UI element was comprised of three modes of interaction, swiping up and down, left and right, hold and rotate. The idea was that the UI element would mimic a mechanical roledex in the first two, and a dimmer switch in the last. I felt this would be a particular challenge, because it would involve some decently complex math and raw css to handle the animation, and the spacial reasoning required to implement this would be pushing the boundaries of what an LLM can do.

